#. the name of this language in the language itself — "Deutsch", not
#. "German". A list of languages is read by the people who speak them.
msgid "English"
msgstr "Deutsch"

#. what this module is called, wherever the interface names it
#: module.yaml
msgid "Create boot medium"
msgstr "Bootmedium erstellen"

#. what it is, in one sentence, under the row that starts the work
#: module.yaml
msgid "Write Arch OS to a USB device to boot another machine from."
msgstr "Arch OS auf einen USB-Datenträger schreiben, um eine andere Maschine davon zu starten."

#. the row that starts the work, and the button on the page before it
#: module.yaml
msgid "Create"
msgstr "Erstellen"

#. ARCH_OS_DOWNLOAD_DIR: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Download folder"
msgstr "Download-Ordner"

#. ARCH_OS_DOWNLOAD_DIR: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Where the image is kept. It is reused, so a second run costs no bandwidth. The folder is created if it is not there, and the image needs about two gigabytes."
msgstr "Wo das Abbild liegt. Es wird wiederverwendet, ein zweiter Lauf kostet also keine Bandbreite. Der Ordner wird angelegt, falls es ihn noch nicht gibt, und das Abbild braucht rund zwei Gigabyte."

#. ARCH_OS_DOWNLOAD_DIR: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Image"
msgstr "Abbild"

#. ARCH_OS_DOWNLOAD_DIR: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Type the full path of a folder, starting with a slash."
msgstr "Gib den vollständigen Pfad eines Ordners an, beginnend mit einem Schrägstrich."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_VERIFY: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Verify checksum"
msgstr "Prüfsumme prüfen"

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_VERIFY: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Holds the image to the checksum its release publishes before anything is written, and throws it away where the two disagree. Turned off, the image in the download folder goes to the device as it is - an image built rather than downloaded is the usual reason."
msgstr "Gleicht das Abbild vor dem Schreiben mit der Prüfsumme ab, die sein Release veröffentlicht, und verwirft es, wenn beide nicht übereinstimmen. Ausgeschaltet geht das Abbild aus dem Download-Ordner unverändert auf das Gerät - der übliche Grund ist ein selbst gebautes statt heruntergeladenes Abbild."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_DEVICE: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Device"
msgstr "Datenträger"

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_DEVICE: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The USB device to write to. Everything on it will be erased. Only USB disks are offered, and none this system is running from, so it cannot be chosen by accident."
msgstr "Der USB-Datenträger, auf den geschrieben wird. Alles darauf wird gelöscht. Angeboten werden nur USB-Datenträger und keiner, von dem dieses System läuft, damit er nicht versehentlich getroffen wird."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_DEVICE: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Choose a device that exists."
msgstr "Wähle einen vorhandenen Datenträger."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_SUDO: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Password for the write"
msgstr "Passwort zum Schreiben"

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_SUDO: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Whether writing the device asks for your password."
msgstr "Ob das Schreiben des Datenträgers nach deinem Passwort fragt."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_PASSWORD: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Your password"
msgstr "Dein Passwort"

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_PASSWORD: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Writing the device needs root, and sudo asks for your password to allow it. It is asked for right before the run starts and is never written to a file."
msgstr "Das Schreiben des Datenträgers braucht Root-Rechte, und sudo fragt dafür nach deinem Passwort. Es wird unmittelbar vor dem Start abgefragt und nie in eine Datei geschrieben."

#. ARCH_OS_IMAGE_PASSWORD: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "That is not your password, or this account may not use sudo."
msgstr "Das ist nicht dein Passwort, oder dieses Konto darf sudo nicht verwenden."

#. ARCH_OS_LOG_URL: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Shared log"
msgstr "Geteiltes Log"

#. ARCH_OS_LOG_URL: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Where the log of a run that failed was put online."
msgstr "Wo das Log eines gescheiterten Laufs online steht."

#. the header's status, while its check says yes
#: ../../oak.yaml
msgid "Online"
msgstr "Online"

#. the header's status, while its check says no
#: ../../oak.yaml
msgid "Offline"
msgstr "Offline"

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@download/image/task.yaml
msgid "Download the image"
msgstr "Abbild herunterladen"

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@verify/checksum/task.yaml
msgid "Verify the checksum"
msgstr "Prüfsumme prüfen"

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@write/device/task.yaml
msgid "Write the image to the device"
msgstr "Abbild auf das Gerät schreiben"

#. read once the step is done, and held on until somebody has
#: tasks/@write/device/task.yaml
msgid ""
"The device is ready\n"
"\n"
"{{ARCH_OS_IMAGE_DEVICE}} now starts Arch OS. Unplug it, plug it into the machine to install, and start that machine from it."
msgstr ""
"Der Datenträger ist fertig\n"
"\n"
"{{ARCH_OS_IMAGE_DEVICE}} startet jetzt Arch OS. Zieh ihn ab, steck ihn in die Maschine, die installiert werden soll, und starte sie davon."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its pages
#: actions/access/action.yaml
msgid "Root for the write"
msgstr "Root zum Schreiben"

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its pages
#: actions/device/action.yaml
msgid "A device to write to"
msgstr "Ein Datenträger zum Schreiben"

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its pages
#: actions/ordinary-machine/action.yaml
msgid "An ordinary Linux machine"
msgstr "Ein gewöhnlicher Linux-Rechner"

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its pages
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid "Share the log"
msgstr "Log teilen"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid "Put the log of this run online, for whoever is helping."
msgstr "Das Log dieses Laufs online stellen, für alle, die helfen."

#. asked before the action runs
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid ""
"Put the log of this run online?\n"
"\n"
"It goes to paste.rs, and its address comes back as a code to scan. Anyone holding that address can read it. It holds every answer but the passwords, which were never written down anywhere."
msgstr ""
"Das Log dieses Laufs online stellen?\n"
"\n"
"Es geht an paste.rs, und seine Adresse kommt als Code zum Scannen zurück. Wer diese Adresse hat, kann es lesen. Es enthält jede Antwort außer den Passwörtern, die nirgends aufgeschrieben wurden."

#. read once the action is done, and held on until somebody has
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid ""
"Log shared\n"
"\n"
"Scan the code, or read the address under it, and hand it to whoever is helping."
msgstr ""
"Log geteilt\n"
"\n"
"Scanne den Code oder lies die Adresse darunter und gib sie an die Person, die dir hilft."
